// Microns Hub wrangler configuration draft (three Workers and one Container app)
// Status: Phase 0 planning deliverable · 2026-09-30 · nothing here is deployed.
// Phase 4 build (2026-10-07): the Phase 4 entries of microns-ops and the microns-mail object below match the built
// workers/ops/wrangler.jsonc and workers/mail/wrangler.jsonc (PLAN.md §5.4, deviations DC-1, DC-2).
// Phase 5 build (2026-10-09): the Phase 5 entries of microns-ops below match the built workers/ops/wrangler.jsonc
// (PLAN.md §5.5, deviations DV5-2, DV5-14, DV5-15, DV5-21): no new Cron Trigger, the image by registry tag, no
// Hyperdrive, the CadContainer class in microns-ops.
// Related: README.md · PLAN.md · ARCHITECTURE.md · INVENTORY.md · inventory.csv · SEO_PARITY.md · AGENTS.md ·
//          RISKS.md · COSTS.md (all in docs/migration/)
//
// =====================================================================================================
// DRAFT. NOT DEPLOYABLE. Never rename this file to wrangler.jsonc and never point wrangler at it.
// =====================================================================================================
// This is one JSONC document. Its top-level keys are the three future config files; each value is a
// complete wrangler configuration object. Keys were checked against the config-schema.json bundled with
// wrangler 4.145.0 (installed 2026-09-30). The document is split like this:
//
//   Future file                   Worker         Created in       Grows in
//   workers/site/wrangler.jsonc   microns-site   Phase 1 (P1-1)   Phase 2 (OPS, R2, rate limits, /api vars), Phase 3 (routes)
//   workers/ops/wrangler.jsonc    microns-ops    Phase 2 (P2-1)   Phase 4 (agent layer), Phase 5 (queues, Workflows, Container)
//   workers/mail/wrangler.jsonc   microns-mail   Phase 4 (P4-4)   -
//   (no file of its own)          microns-cad    Phase 5 (P5-6)   Container stanza in microns-ops, which exports
//                                                                 the CadContainer class (source in
//                                                                 workers/ops/src/cad-container; workers/cad holds
//                                                                 the README and the parity tool)
//
// Conventions
// - "Phase N" next to an entry = the phase in which the entry is added to the real file. When a file is
//   first created, copy only the entries of the current and earlier phases: a binding to a Worker, queue,
//   index, Hyperdrive config or container image that does not exist yet makes the deploy fail.
// - Kept as comments on purpose, because enabling them changes production behaviour instead of adding an
//   idle binding: the Phase 3 routes (they take production traffic; PLAN.md §6 runbook S11-S14) and the
//   optional Phase 7 D1 entries. The Phase 5 jobs need no cron entry: they are rows of a schedule table read by
//   the every-minute trigger, each switched on by its flag at P5-8 (PLAN.md §5.5 DV5-2). The Phase 4 mcp.micronshub.eu Custom Domain is active in the built ops file:
//   it serves only the remote MCP host, which offers a status tool alone until the flag mcp.remote is on.
// - IDs are placeholders in angle brackets, for example "<KV_ID_SEO_CACHE>". Replace them with the IDs that
//   `wrangler kv namespace create`, `wrangler hyperdrive create` and the dashboard print. A placeholder is
//   never replaced by a secret value.
// - account_id is not set: CI passes CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID (GitHub secret, PLAN.md P0-8).
// - Evidence tags follow PLAN.md: path:line = this repository at commit 9afcba8; "live 2026-09-30";
//   "CF docs (verified 2026-09-27)" = checked during planning (README.md §11); "CF docs (verified 2026-09-30)"
//   = checked while writing this draft; "CF docs, re-check at execution" = not verified yet. The component,
//   binding target, queue, Workflow and Durable Object class names are the canonical ones of ARCHITECTURE.md;
//   binding variable names that ARCHITECTURE.md does not fix (queues, Workflows, Durable Objects) are set here.
// - No send_email binding anywhere: outbound mail stays on Resend (brief §2 item 4).
//
// Secrets: NAMES ONLY. Values are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>` in the Worker's folder (or in the
// dashboard), never in a file: the repository is public. Every secret set is appended to the P0-2 consumer
// checklist the same day (PLAN.md P0-2, P2-9) and rotated in P6-1. Each object below also carries
// "secrets": { "required": [...] }; with it, `wrangler deploy` and `wrangler versions upload` fail when a
// listed secret is missing on the Worker (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30).
//
//   microns-site  Phase 1: SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
//                 Phase 2: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY, TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY, R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID,
//                          R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, LEGACY_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, LEGACY_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
//                          ACCESS_MACHINE_CLIENT_IDS
//                 Phase 4 (optional, not in secrets.required): AGENT_APPROVAL_SECRET (relay signature check)
//                 Phase 5 (optional, not in secrets.required): CAD_COMPAT_TOKEN (path token of the CAD compat route)
//   microns-ops   Phase 2: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY, RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
//                          TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET,
//                          GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI, APOLLO_API_KEY, GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON (reserved; note in the ops secrets block)
//                 Phase 4 (optional, not in secrets.required, checked where used): AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN, CAD_UNFOLD_URL,
//                          CAD_SHARED_SECRET, AGENT_APPROVAL_SECRET, CAD_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID and CAD_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET
//                          (only with the CAD network path chosen at OW-11). ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set (AI Gateway
//                          BYOK) and no MCP_OAUTH_* secret exists (stateless MCP handler + Access Managed OAuth, DC-1)
//                 Phase 5 (optional, not in secrets.required, checked where used): INDEXNOW_KEY, XOMETRY_TOKEN,
//                          XOMETRY_COOKIE. No GEMINI_API_KEY: the Google AI Studio key is stored in AI Gateway
//   microns-mail  Phase 4: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY; optional MAIL_COPY_TO, MAIL_FALLBACK_TO (verified destination
//                          addresses, secrets so that no address sits in the repository)
//
// Where today's names differ (for the P0-2 checklist): the Xometry scanner reads XB_PARTNER_AUTH_TOKEN
// (xometry-bot/xometry_bot/config.py:153) and xometry-review reads XOMETRY_PARTNER_AUTH_TOKEN
// (supabase/functions/xometry-review/index.ts:196); both become XOMETRY_TOKEN on the Worker. The legacy S3
// pair replaces AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY and their VITE_-prefixed fallbacks (api/s3.js:47-52).
// The articles scope can use its own pair on Vercel, AWS_ARTICLES_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_ARTICLES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
// (api/s3.js:53-64); the Phase 2 site Worker uses the one LEGACY_AWS_* pair for both legacy scopes (rfq, and
// articles until P3-6), so its key is created for both buckets (P0-4 lists the Vercel names).
{
  // ===================================================================================================
  // microns-site: Static Assets, SEO handler, redirect table, sitemap routes, /api/* router
  // ===================================================================================================
  "workers/site/wrangler.jsonc": {
    "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
    "name": "microns-site",
    // Router order (PLAN.md P1-3): redirect table -> sitemap routes -> /api/* -> SEO handler for /{lang}
    // and /{lang}/* -> directory-index emulation (only if the baseline shows it) -> env.ASSETS.fetch(request).
    "main": "src/index.ts",
    // Set to the scaffolding date at P1-1; it must stay >= 2025-04-01 (see the flag note below).
    "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
    "compatibility_flags": [
      // nodejs_compat: the ported handlers use Buffer, node:crypto and the Resend SDK (H-20; for example
      // api/marketing.js:9, :25 and api/emails.js:12, :290), and read process.env at module scope. With
      // nodejs_compat, nodejs_compat_populate_process_env is on by default for compatibility dates on or
      // after 2025-04-01 and exposes vars and secrets through process.env (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30),
      // so no second flag is listed.
      "nodejs_compat"
    ],
    // Phase 1 serves only here: microns-site.<WORKERS_SUBDOMAIN>.workers.dev, behind Cloudflare Access with a
    // service token for the parity tool, Playwright and Lighthouse (P1-7), and always with X-Robots-Tag: noindex.
    "workers_dev": true,
    // Version and alias URLs for `wrangler versions upload --preview-alias staging` (P1-9). Possible here
    // because this Worker has no Durable Objects; version URLs are not generated for Workers that implement
    // Durable Objects (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30).
    "preview_urls": true,
    // Workers Logs at full sampling: the Phase 3 gate needs "zero 5xx on SEO paths" as evidence.
    "observability": {
      "enabled": true,
      "head_sampling_rate": 1
    },

    // Phase 1. Vite writes the build to dist/ (no outDir in vite.config.ts:119-120); the path is relative
    // to workers/site/.
    "assets": {
      "directory": "../../dist",
      "binding": "ASSETS",
      // "none": exact file paths such as /index.html and /laserkritis/index.html are served as they are,
      // and everything else goes to not_found_handling. The default "auto-trailing-slash" would answer
      // /index.html with a 307 to / and /en with a 307 to /en/ (CF docs, verified 2026-09-27), which breaks
      // URL parity and the shell fetch described below.
      "html_handling": "none",
      // Unknown paths get /index.html with 200, like the Vercel SPA fallback "/(.*)" -> "/index.html"
      // (vercel.json:158-161). This is soft-404 parity (H-9); real 404s come from the Worker once the flag
      // seo.strict_404 is on, never from the asset layer.
      "not_found_handling": "single-page-application",
      // true: every request reaches the Worker first, as on Vercel, where middleware.ts runs before the
      // 210 prerendered files and shadows them (H-8). The SEO handler takes the shell from
      // env.ASSETS.fetch(new URL('/index.html', url)), because a Worker cannot fetch its own hostname
      // (H-4; today middleware.ts:424 does exactly that on Vercel). A glob array is allowed later to save
      // requests, but every /{lang} path must stay Worker-first.
      "run_worker_first": true
    },
    // No _redirects and no _headers file in dist/:
    // - public/_redirects:1 ("/*  /index.html  200", Netlify syntax, inert on Vercel) is deleted in P1-2 (H-3).
    //   Static Assets would apply it inside the asset layer to every request the Worker hands to ASSETS,
    //   whether or not an asset matches (CF docs, verified 2026-09-27), overriding the Worker's decision.
    // - The 25 redirects of vercel.json:2-128 and the 3 client-only entries of
    //   src/components/SEORedirects.tsx:14-73 live in workers/site/src/redirects.ts instead: status 308 (what
    //   Vercel emits for permanent: true), matched on the raw and the NFC-decoded path, with the dead mojibake
    //   source kept byte-identical. _redirects cannot do the NFC matching and defaults to 302.
    // - _headers is optional (immutable caching of /assets/* only). CORS on /api/* is emitted by the Worker
    //   with the same values as vercel.json:163-172 (H-28).

    "kv_namespaces": [
      // Phase 1. SEO row cache shared by all isolates (1 h TTL), behind the per-isolate Map caches ported
      // from middleware.ts. KV's minimum expirationTtl is 60 s (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30), so the 30 s
      // negative entries stay in the Map, or are stored with their own timestamp and checked on read.
      { "binding": "SEO_CACHE", "id": "<KV_ID_SEO_CACHE>" },
      // Phase 1. Feature flags read on each request (seo.strict_404, api.forward_to_vercel). Set by hand
      // until Phase 4, then mirrored every minute from table feature_flags by microns-ops (P4-2).
      { "binding": "FLAGS", "id": "<KV_ID_FLAGS>" }
    ],

    "services": [
      // Phase 2. /api/* endpoints that microns-site does not serve itself go to microns-ops (PLAN.md §5.2
      // route table) as an RPC call to the named entrypoint OpsApi: handle(request, call). The verified caller
      // and the function URL travel in `call`, never in headers. microns-ops is deployed before this Worker.
      { "binding": "OPS", "service": "microns-ops", "entrypoint": "OpsApi" }
    ],

    "r2_buckets": [
      // Phase 2. Files of the /api/s3 replacement (workers/site/src/api/files.ts): new uploads under rfq/ +
      // today's key (<rfqNumber>/<partFolder>/<safeName>, so the browser keeps the key it gets today; PLAN.md
      // §5.2 DV-5), and the per-folder upload counters under upload-counters/. Phase 4 e-mail RFQs use
      // rfq/<rfq_id>/<file_id>-<name>. Browser uploads use presigned URLs (aws4fetch against the R2 S3 API with
      // R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY); the binding serves head, list and delete. The bucket has no
      // public access and no custom domain. Jurisdiction eu: chosen only when the bucket is created
      // (`wrangler r2 bucket create microns-private -J eu`, P2-9); every binding of the bucket carries it, and
      // R2_JURISDICTION in files.ts must match (a config test checks it). Owner decision D-1.
      { "binding": "PRIVATE_FILES", "bucket_name": "microns-private", "jurisdiction": "eu" }
    ],

    "ratelimits": [
      // Phase 2. Workers Rate Limiting bindings for /api/* (P2-7). namespace_id is a positive integer as a
      // string, chosen by us and unique in the account (the same id shares its counters across Workers);
      // period is 10 or 60 s. Counters are per Cloudflare location and eventually consistent (CF docs, verified
      // 2026-09-30), so this complements Turnstile and the zone rate-limiting rule of Phase 3. MAIL takes the
      // mail keys; BULK takes idempotent reads and upload presigns (pages presign every file of an RFQ at once);
      // the code falls back to API_RATE_LIMIT when MAIL or BULK is absent. Namespaces go into the P0-2 checklist.
      { "name": "API_RATE_LIMIT", "namespace_id": "2001", "simple": { "limit": 30, "period": 60 } },
      { "name": "API_RATE_LIMIT_MAIL", "namespace_id": "2002", "simple": { "limit": 5, "period": 60 } },
      { "name": "API_RATE_LIMIT_BULK", "namespace_id": "2003", "simple": { "limit": 300, "period": 60 } }
    ],

    // Phase 7 (optional, owner decision 2026-09-30): SEO reads move from Supabase REST to D1 (P7-8).
    // "d1_databases": [
    //   { "binding": "DB", "database_name": "microns-db", "database_id": "<D1_ID_MICRONS_DB>" }
    // ],

    "vars": {
      // Phase 1. Replaces the literal at middleware.ts:43 (a project URL, not a secret).
      "SUPABASE_URL": "https://cfjrtmtaitwzggzpkhxi.supabase.co",
      // Phase 1. Production origin: canonical and hreflang host, sitemap <loc> host.
      "SITE_ORIGIN": "https://www.micronshub.eu",
      // Phase 1. Comma-separated non-production hosts. The Worker adds X-Robots-Tag: noindex on these and
      // on any *.workers.dev host (P1-7). Alias hosts have the form <alias>-<worker>.<subdomain>.workers.dev
      // (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30).
      "PREVIEW_HOSTNAMES": "microns-site.<WORKERS_SUBDOMAIN>.workers.dev,staging-microns-site.<WORKERS_SUBDOMAIN>.workers.dev",
      // Phase 1. Deploy-time default of flag seo.strict_404 (a value in KV FLAGS wins). "false" keeps the
      // soft-404 parity with Vercel (H-9); switched only after PLAN.md Q5 (P3-7).
      "SEO_STRICT_404": "false",
      // Phase 1 var, Phase 2 value. Target of the /api forward (paths outside the /api catalogue, and every
      // /api request while api.forward_to_vercel is on): the Vercel deployment host, not www, because once the
      // Phase 3 routes send www to this Worker the forward refuses to call its own host.
      "API_FORWARD_ORIGIN": "https://on-demand-craft-greece.vercel.app",
      // Phase 2. Fallback of the KV flag api.forward_to_vercel: "true" forwards every /api request.
      "API_FORWARD_TO_VERCEL": "false",
      // Phase 2. Account ID for the R2 S3 API endpoint used when presigning (not a secret); with jurisdiction eu
      // the endpoint is https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.eu.r2.cloudflarestorage.com.
      "R2_ACCOUNT_ID": "<CF_ACCOUNT_ID>",
      // Phase 2. Region and names of the legacy S3 buckets (H-17; api/s3.js:28-45): no new rfq uploads; the
      // articles scope stays there until P3-6 (owner decision D-17). Names come from P0-4; they are not secret.
      "LEGACY_S3_REGION": "eu-north-1",
      "LEGACY_S3_RFQ_BUCKET": "<LEGACY_S3_RFQ_BUCKET>",
      "LEGACY_S3_ARTICLES_BUCKET": "<LEGACY_S3_ARTICLES_BUCKET>",
      // Phase 2. Cloudflare Access team domain and the audience tag of the Access application in front of the
      // machine callers' host (preview in Phase 2).
      "ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN": "<ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN>",
      "ACCESS_AUD": "<ACCESS_AUD_PREVIEW>",
      // Phase 2. Gate mode per class, "<class>=report|enforce" comma list; a class not named enforces. The
      // production value is set by the Phase 3 runbook (owner decision D-16).
      "API_GATES_MODE": "recipient=report",
      // Phase 2. Hosts besides the preview hosts that accept machine callers (exact match, comma list). Empty in
      // Phase 2; the Phase 3 runbook sets "api.micronshub.eu" (owner decision D-3).
      "API_MACHINE_HOSTS": ""
    },

    "secrets": {
      "required": [
        // Phase 1. SEO reads; today read from process.env with a silent empty fallback (middleware.ts:103-109).
        // The Worker fails loudly instead when it is missing (P1-4).
        "SUPABASE_ANON_KEY",
        // Phase 2 (site-local /api/* subset: emails, files, track; the gates; PLAN.md §5.2). The Worker checks
        // the names each request needs, so a missing one fails only those requests; a deploy fails while one is unset.
        "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY",
        "RESEND_API_KEY",
        "TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY",
        "R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID",
        "R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY",
        "LEGACY_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID",
        "LEGACY_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY",
        // Phase 2. "<client-id>=collector,<client-id>=mcp": maps each machine service token to its consumer.
        "ACCESS_MACHINE_CLIENT_IDS"
        // Phase 4. AGENT_APPROVAL_SECRET (relay signature check on /api/agent/decision) is optional and checked per
        // request, so it is not listed: a site deploy never fails for agent configuration (PLAN.md §5.4 DF-72).
        // Phase 5. CAD_COMPAT_TOKEN (gate CD-1 of /api/cad/<token>/flat-pattern) is optional for the same reason;
        // without it the route answers 500 (PLAN.md §5.5).
      ]
    },

    // Phase 3 (runbook S11): empty until the zone is on Cloudflare. Routes are inert while the records are
    // DNS only; the flips at S12 (www) and S14 (wildcard) make them live. The apex is not a route: it is a
    // Single Redirect Rule to https://www.micronshub.eu${path}${query} with the status seen in the baseline.
    // www uses a Route on a proxied placeholder record, not a Custom Domain: a Custom Domain cannot be created
    // while www has a CNAME, and a Route keeps rollback a single record flip (CF docs, verified 2026-09-27).
    // The most specific pattern wins, so www.micronshub.eu/* beats *.micronshub.eu/* (CF docs, verified
    // 2026-09-30).
    // Routes run in front of Custom Domains: "A Worker running on a Custom Domain is treated as an origin"
    // (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30). The wildcard route would therefore also catch mcp.micronshub.eu
    // (Custom Domain of microns-ops) and, by the same logic, files.micronshub.eu (R2 custom domain; CF docs,
    // re-check at execution). At S11 add dashboard routes mcp.micronshub.eu/* and files.micronshub.eu/* with
    // Worker "None" (a route without a Worker cannot be written in this file), or have the router pass those
    // hosts through with fetch(request).
    "routes": [
      // { "pattern": "www.micronshub.eu/*", "zone_name": "micronshub.eu" },
      // { "pattern": "*.micronshub.eu/*", "zone_name": "micronshub.eu" }
    ]
  },

  // ===================================================================================================
  // microns-ops: ops/admin API (Hono), Cron Triggers, Queue consumers, Workflows, Durable Objects,
  // Container, Vectorize, AI Gateway, Browser Rendering, remote MCP on mcp.micronshub.eu (stateless handler, no DO)
  // ===================================================================================================
  "workers/ops/wrangler.jsonc": {
    "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
    "name": "microns-ops",
    // Hono app inside the named entrypoint OpsApi (RPC handle(request, call) from microns-site; the default
    // fetch answers 404). Routes run api/*.js unchanged through workers/ops/src/compat/express-shim.ts, the Hono
    // adapter over the shared @vercel/node shim (workers/shared/src/compat/vercel-node.ts). Plus the queue()
    // handler (Phase 2) and scheduled() (Phase 4); exports the Workflow, Durable Object and Container classes
    // listed below and (Phase 4) the named entrypoint MailIngest (RPC startIntake, ingestReply from microns-mail).
    // Phase 4: the default fetch serves the remote MCP when the host is MCP_HOSTNAME and keeps the 404 otherwise.
    "main": "src/index.ts",
    "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
    "compatibility_flags": [
      // node:crypto createSign RSA-SHA256 for the Google service-account token (api/_lib/gsc-client.js:18,
      // :131), createHmac, Buffer and module-scope process.env in api/*.js and lib/* (H-20).
      "nodejs_compat"
    ],
    // No public workers.dev host: reached only through the OPS service binding, Cron and Queue triggers,
    // and (Phase 4) the mcp.micronshub.eu Custom Domain.
    "workers_dev": false,
    // Version URLs are not generated for Workers with Durable Objects or Containers (CF docs, verified
    // 2026-09-30).
    "preview_urls": false,
    "observability": {
      "enabled": true,
      "head_sampling_rate": 1
    },
    // Phase 2. /api/notifications?action=nest runs the nesting engine synchronously. Its 50 s budget
    // (lib/nesting/nester.js:286) never trips when deployed, because Date.now() advances only on I/O, and local
    // CPU passes 30 s near 700 part instances (probe 2026-10-02); the default CPU limit is 30 s and the maximum
    // 300,000 ms (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30). The limit applies to every invocation of this Worker, queue
    // consumers included; it is a runaway guard (CPU is billed as used). An OPS rejection on nest answers 504
    // TIMEOUT in microns-site. PLAN.md §5.2 DV-4.
    "limits": {
      "cpu_ms": 300000
    },
    // Phase 2. lib/inventory needs qrcode's server build (toBuffer); without the alias the bundler picks the
    // browser build. Relative to workers/ops/ (repo root node_modules).
    "alias": {
      "qrcode": "./../../node_modules/qrcode/lib/server.js"
    },

    "vars": {
      // Phase 2. Not in the planned binding list for microns-ops; added because the ported code needs them.
      // ARCHITECTURE.md should list them too.
      "SUPABASE_URL": "https://cfjrtmtaitwzggzpkhxi.supabase.co",
      "SITE_ORIGIN": "https://www.micronshub.eu",
      // Phase 4. AI Gateway id. The gateway has no binding of its own: Anthropic calls use the provider-native URL
      // from env.AI.gateway(AI_GATEWAY_ID).getUrl('anthropic'), embeddings env.AI.run with the gateway option; routes
      // extract, classify, embed (translate in Phase 5); each call carries cf-aig-metadata with five keys (agent,
      // run_id, tenant_id, step, prompt) and payload logging off (ARCHITECTURE.md §13; P4-3).
      "AI_GATEWAY_ID": "microns",
      // Phase 4. Default tenant of agent rows; quote sender identity and our Message-ID domain; default CAD backend
      // (stays "vps" in the merged file; the owner sets "container" at switch-over step S9); remote MCP host and route; Access identifiers of the MCP application (not
      // secrets; placeholders replaced at OW-5 and OW-15); crawler identity and the owner-recorded host permissions
      // of the scrapers (JSON host -> permission reference; empty = no host permitted). Local-test overrides
      // (AGENT_STUBS, AGENT_LLM_BASE_URL, *_API_BASE, GOOGLE_TOKEN_URL) never appear here: the bundle check refuses them.
      "AGENT_TENANT_ID": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
      "QUOTE_FROM": "MicronsHub Quotations <info@micronshub.eu>",
      "QUOTE_REPLY_TO": "replies@rfq.micronshub.eu",
      "MESSAGE_ID_DOMAIN": "rfq.micronshub.eu",
      "CAD_BACKEND_DEFAULT": "vps",
      "MCP_HOSTNAME": "mcp.micronshub.eu",
      "MCP_ROUTE": "/mcp",
      "ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN": "<ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN>",
      "MCP_ACCESS_AUD": "<ACCESS_AUD_MCP>",
      "SCRAPER_USER_AGENT": "MicronsHubBot/1.0 (+https://www.micronshub.eu/en/contact)",
      "SCRAPER_PERMITTED_HOSTS": "{}",
      // Phase 5 (P5-2, P5-4, P5-6, P5-7). Tracking links keep the apex host of the repo send-campaign function; the
      // digest sender identity. Marketing switches: anything but "true" is off; PAUSED = rollback to the edge path
      // (route 503, the dashboard falls back), STOPPED = no campaign mail at all (route 423, queued mail held).
      // CAD_SLOTS must equal containers[0].max_instances; CAD_INPUT_HOSTS = the exact presign hosts of the RFQ
      // storage (comma list, set at deploy time); keep-warm off. The T2-only overrides (PULLPUSH_API_BASE,
      // HN_API_BASE, XOMETRY_API_BASE, INDEXNOW_API_BASE, AGENT_GEMINI_BASE_URL, CAD_CONTAINER_BASE_URL,
      // CONTENT_WAIT_TIMEOUT_S) never appear here: the bundle check refuses them.
      "TRACKING_DOMAIN": "https://micronshub.eu",
      "DIGEST_FROM": "MicronsHub Ops <info@micronshub.eu>",
      "MARKETING_FOLLOWUPS_ENABLED": "false",
      "MARKETING_WARMUP_ENABLED": "false",
      "OUTBOUND_MAIL_PAUSED": "false",
      "OUTBOUND_MAIL_STOPPED": "false",
      "CAD_SLOTS": "3",
      "CAD_INPUT_HOSTS": "<CAD_INPUT_HOSTS>",
      "CAD_PROCESSING_TIMEOUT_S": "120",
      "CAD_KEEP_WARM": "off"
    },

    "kv_namespaces": [
      // Phase 4 (agent flags, read with cacheTtl 30 s and fail closed; writer: the every-minute cron mirrors table
      // feature_flags here by revision, plus write-through on dashboard edits, P4-2). api.forward_to_vercel stays a
      // microns-site read. Same namespace as microns-site.
      { "binding": "FLAGS", "id": "<KV_ID_FLAGS>" },
      // Phase 5. Purge of SEO entries when content-daily publishes (same namespace as microns-site).
      // KV allows 1 write per second to the same key (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30); purges are per key.
      { "binding": "SEO_CACHE", "id": "<KV_ID_SEO_CACHE>" }
    ],

    "r2_buckets": [
      // Phase 4. Prefixes email/<message_id_sha256>/..., rfq/<rfq_id>/<file_id>-<name>, cad/<job_id>/output/...,
      // quotes/<rfq_id>/v<version>/quote.pdf, orders/<order_id>/traveler.pdf, eval/golden/...; Phase 5 adds
      // sitemaps/sitemap-complete.xml (a shadow copy: Supabase Storage stays the served source, DV5-1) and
      // phase5-shadow/... (outputs of runs in shadow mode). Same jurisdiction as the site binding.
      { "binding": "PRIVATE_FILES", "bucket_name": "microns-private", "jurisdiction": "eu" }
      // Later (not added in Phase 5: no consumer yet, PLAN.md §5.5 M-3). Public objects behind the R2 custom domain
      // files.micronshub.eu (connected in P3-6): articles/<yyyy>/<mm>/<slug>.<ext>, tenants/<slug>/... Customer
      // files never go here.
      // { "binding": "PUBLIC_FILES", "bucket_name": "microns-public" }
    ],

    // Queue binding names are this draft's choice (the queue names are canonical). Dead-letter queues
    // <name>-dlq are created automatically when first named (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30). They have no
    // consumer: the ops digest reports their depth and a manual task re-drives them.
    "queues": {
      "producers": [
        // Phase 2. Tender scans started by a machine caller (/api/tender-scan POST; answered 200 with queued and
        // run_id). Staff scans, the funded-startups scan and GSC bulk actions stay synchronous in Phase 2 (P2-6,
        // PLAN.md §5.2 DV-3). Phase 4 adds directory scans in their own envelope (kind directory-scan); Phase 5 adds
        // the scheduled collectors and the Xometry scan in theirs (P5ScrapeMessage: reddit-tier, hn-scan,
        // tender-scheduled, xometry-scan); the Phase 2 message and consumer stay unchanged. The GSC and funded-scan
        // queue kinds were not built in Phase 5 (PLAN.md §5.5 BA5-10).
        { "binding": "SCRAPES", "queue": "scrapes" },
        // Phase 4. CAD analysis jobs from rfq-intake and quote (P4-6).
        { "binding": "CAD_JOBS", "queue": "cad-jobs" },
        // Phase 4. Agent events: inbound-reply, order-created, resume-parked, card (AGENTS.md §4).
        { "binding": "AGENT_EVENTS", "queue": "agent-events" },
        // Phase 5. One message per article and language (P5-2; fixes the translation lag of H-19).
        { "binding": "TRANSLATIONS", "queue": "translations" },
        // Phase 5. One message per campaign recipient; pacing per sender in SenderLimiter (P5-4).
        { "binding": "OUTBOUND_MAIL", "queue": "outbound-mail" }
      ],
      // Batch sizes, retries and concurrency are starting values, tuned when each consumer ships.
      // Defaults are batch 10, timeout 5 s, 3 retries (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30); a consumer invocation
      // may keep at most 6 connections waiting for response headers (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30).
      "consumers": [
        {
          // Phase 2. One scan per message: scans are long and hit third-party sites. A failed scan is retried
          // after 300 s, three times, then kept in scrapes-dlq. Consumer kinds built: tender-scan, funded-scan.
          "queue": "scrapes",
          "max_batch_size": 1,
          "max_retries": 3,
          "max_concurrency": 2,
          "retry_delay": 300,
          "dead_letter_queue": "scrapes-dlq"
        },
        {
          // Phase 4. One CAD job per message; concurrency equals the Container max_instances below,
          // because each instance runs one synchronous uvicorn worker (README.md §7 item 3). The consumer runs the
          // job under a CadRouter lease, which limits each backend further (Phase 4: unfold service 1, inline 1).
          "queue": "cad-jobs",
          "max_batch_size": 1,
          "max_retries": 2,
          "max_concurrency": 3,
          "dead_letter_queue": "cad-jobs-dlq"
        },
        {
          // Phase 4. Per-message ack or retry.
          "queue": "agent-events",
          "max_batch_size": 25,
          "max_batch_timeout": 10,
          "max_retries": 3,
          "dead_letter_queue": "agent-events-dlq"
        },
        {
          // Phase 5. One language per message, up to three at once; retried 5 times, 120 s apart (120 s x attempts
          // when every model of the chain is overloaded), then kept in translations-dlq.
          "queue": "translations",
          "max_batch_size": 1,
          "max_retries": 5,
          "retry_delay": 120,
          "max_concurrency": 3,
          "dead_letter_queue": "translations-dlq"
        },
        {
          // Phase 5. The SenderLimiter Durable Object enforces per-sender pacing; the queue only buffers. Messages of a
          // batch are sent one after another; a cap or spacing wait is a delayed re-send, never a retry.
          "queue": "outbound-mail",
          "max_batch_size": 10,
          "max_retries": 3,
          "retry_delay": 60,
          "max_concurrency": 2,
          "dead_letter_queue": "outbound-mail-dlq"
        }
      ]
    },

    // Workflow binding names are this draft's choice (names and classes are canonical). Workflow-level
    // "schedules" exist in the wrangler 4.145.0 schema but are not used: one scheduled() dispatcher keeps
    // the flag check and the agent_runs row in one place.
    "workflows": [
      // Phase 4 (P4-5). Started by microns-mail through the OPS service binding.
      { "name": "rfq-intake", "binding": "RFQ_INTAKE", "class_name": "RfqIntakeWorkflow" },
      // Phase 4 (P4-7). waitForEvent type "quote-approved": event types allow letters, digits, - and _ only
      // (CF docs, verified 2026-09-27).
      { "name": "quote", "binding": "QUOTE", "class_name": "QuoteWorkflow" },
      // Phase 4 (P4-9).
      { "name": "post-order", "binding": "POST_ORDER", "class_name": "PostOrderWorkflow" },
      // Phase 5 (P5-2). Generate, translate (queue translations; IndexNow per translation in the consumer), fix
      // links, sitemap.
      { "name": "content-daily", "binding": "CONTENT_DAILY", "class_name": "ContentDailyWorkflow" },
      // Phase 5 (P5-2). Writes the Supabase Storage object the site serves plus an R2 shadow copy (DV5-1).
      { "name": "sitemap", "binding": "SITEMAP", "class_name": "SitemapWorkflow" },
      // Phase 5 (P5-7).
      { "name": "ops-digest", "binding": "OPS_DIGEST", "class_name": "OpsDigestWorkflow" }
    ],

    // Durable Object binding names are this draft's choice (the classes are canonical).
    "durable_objects": {
      "bindings": [
        // Phase 4. One per RFQ (name = rfq_id).
        { "name": "RFQ_THREAD", "class_name": "RfqThread" },
        // Phase 4. One per material/stock key: a single writer per material prevents double-booking (P4-9).
        { "name": "MATERIAL_STOCK", "class_name": "MaterialStock" },
        // Phase 4. Lease and health coordinator of the CAD backends (the existing unfold service and the inline
        // backend until Phase 5, then CadContainer); the cad-jobs consumer runs the job (P4-6, DC-3).
        { "name": "CAD_ROUTER", "class_name": "CadRouter" },
        // No MCP_OBJECT / MicronsMcp: the remote MCP is the stateless createMcpHandler of the Agents SDK in the default
        // fetch (McpAgent is deprecated and feature-frozen, CF docs fetched 2026-10-03; DC-1).
        // Phase 5. One per sender account (P5-4).
        { "name": "SENDER_LIMITER", "class_name": "SenderLimiter" },
        // Phase 5. Container-enabled Durable Object class of microns-cad (P5-6), exported by microns-ops from
        // src/cad-container/ together with ContainerProxy (one copy of @cloudflare/containers 0.3.7).
        { "name": "CAD_CONTAINER", "class_name": "CadContainer" }
      ]
    },
    // Append-only: a tag is never edited or reused after it has been deployed. All classes use SQLite-backed
    // storage, which Containers and the Agents SDK expect (CF docs, re-check at execution).
    // CF docs (verified 2026-09-30) now show a declarative "exports" block, for example
    // "exports": { "RfqThread": { "type": "durable-object", "storage": "sqlite" } }, and call "migrations" the
    // legacy form: it keeps working, but the two cannot be combined in one Worker. Phase 4 chose "migrations"
    // (workers/ops/wrangler.jsonc); never mix the two forms.
    "migrations": [
      // Phase 4 (deployed once, then never edited).
      { "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["RfqThread", "MaterialStock", "CadRouter"] },
      // Phase 5: both classes in one deploy, after the CAD image was pushed.
      { "tag": "v2", "new_sqlite_classes": ["SenderLimiter", "CadContainer"] }
    ],

    "containers": [
      {
        // Phase 5 (P5-6). Component microns-cad: sheet-metal-service (uvicorn on port 8000). As built the image is
        // built from sheet-metal-service/Dockerfile (linux/amd64), tested and pushed by .github/workflows/cad-image.yml
        // and referenced by its registry tag exactly as `wrangler containers push` prints it, so an ops deploy needs
        // no Docker (PLAN.md §5.5 DV5-14). The port, sleepAfter (10 min), no internet, the ping path and the
        // CAD_SHARED_SECRET handed to the container are set in the CadContainer class, not here.
        "name": "microns-cad",
        "class_name": "CadContainer",
        "image": "registry.cloudflare.com/<CF_ACCOUNT_ID>/microns-cad:<IMAGE_TAG>",
        // standard-1 = 1/2 vCPU, 4 GiB memory, 8 GB disk; standard-2 = 1 vCPU, 6 GiB, 12 GB if unfold times
        // need it (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30).
        "instance_type": "standard-1",
        // Equals max_concurrency of the cad-jobs consumer (README.md §7 item 3: 2-3 instances) and the var CAD_SLOTS.
        "max_instances": 3
      }
    ],

    "vectorize": [
      // Phase 4. RAG over past won/lost quotes (one vector per quote line, namespace = tenant). Create with
      // `wrangler vectorize create quotes-v1 --dimensions=1024 --metric=cosine` (bge-m3 embeddings), then the metadata
      // indexes (process, material_family, outcome, thickness_mm, sent_at_unix) before any insert (OW-4).
      { "binding": "QUOTES_INDEX", "index_name": "quotes-v1" }
    ],

    // Phase 4. Workers AI (@cf/baai/bge-m3 for the embed route) and access to AI Gateway "microns".
    "ai": { "binding": "AI" },

    // Phase 4 (P4-10). Europages and wlw scrapers: only client-rendered pages of owner-permitted hosts, after the
    // robots.txt gate; one browser per invocation; at most 6 concurrent connections per invocation.
    "browser": { "binding": "BROWSER" },

    // Phase 4 (P4-11). Remote MCP calls per user; namespace on the P0-2 checklist.
    "ratelimits": [
      { "name": "MCP_RATE_LIMIT", "namespace_id": "2004", "simple": { "limit": 60, "period": 60 } }
    ],

    // Phase 4. Prompt files are bundled as text, PDF fonts and the logo as bytes.
    "rules": [
      { "type": "Data", "globs": ["**/*.ttf", "**/*.png"], "fallthrough": true },
      { "type": "Text", "globs": ["**/*.md"], "fallthrough": true }
    ],

    // Phase 5, optional (P5-5), not created (PLAN.md §5.5 DV5-15): the Xometry scan writes xometry_offers through
    // PostgREST with the service role, so no database password leaves Supabase. Kept as a comment for reference.
    // "hyperdrive": [
    //   { "binding": "SUPABASE_DB", "id": "<HYPERDRIVE_ID_SUPABASE_DB>" }
    // ],

    "analytics_engine_datasets": [
      // Phase 4 (P4-13). Data points llm_call, embed_call, step, run_end, cad_job, mail_in, send (index run_id);
      // Phase 5 adds cad_compat and xometry_tick.
      { "binding": "EVENTS", "dataset": "microns_events" }
    ],

    // Phase 7 (optional, owner decision 2026-09-30): data API /api/data/* on D1 (P7-1, P7-2); migrations
    // managed with `wrangler d1 migrations` in workers/ops/migrations/.
    // "d1_databases": [
    //   {
    //     "binding": "DB",
    //     "database_name": "microns-db",
    //     "database_id": "<D1_ID_MICRONS_DB>",
    //     "migrations_dir": "migrations"
    //   }
    // ],

    "secrets": {
      "required": [
        // Phase 2 (ops/admin API routes: gsc, tenders, tender-scan, scrape-*, scan-directory, funded-startups,
        // marketing webhook/google-auth/apollo-enrich, inv-*, nest).
        "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY",
        "SUPABASE_ANON_KEY",
        "RESEND_API_KEY",
        "RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET",
        "TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN",
        "TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID",
        "GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID",
        "GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET",
        // Replaces the VERCEL_URL-derived default of api/marketing.js:46-47.
        "GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI",
        "APOLLO_API_KEY"
        // Reserved, not required: the GSC client reads its Google credentials from the database
        // (api/_lib/gsc-client.js:4), not from env. Add it only if they move to a Worker secret.
        // "GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON",
        // Not listed on purpose: a listed secret that does not exist on the Worker makes every deploy fail, so the
        // Phase 4 and Phase 5 secrets are optional and checked where they are used (PLAN.md §5.2 DV-9, §5.4 DF-72):
        // Phase 4 AI_GATEWAY_TOKEN, CAD_UNFOLD_URL, CAD_SHARED_SECRET, AGENT_APPROVAL_SECRET, CAD_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID,
        // CAD_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET; Phase 5 INDEXNOW_KEY, XOMETRY_TOKEN, XOMETRY_COOKIE (no GEMINI_API_KEY: BYOK).
        // ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set (BYOK) and no MCP_OAUTH_* secret exists (DC-1).
      ]
    },

    "triggers": {
      // UTC: "Cron Triggers execute on UTC time" (CF docs, verified 2026-09-30). One scheduled() handler
      // dispatches on controller.cron; every job checks its flag in KV FLAGS and writes an agent_runs row
      // (H-29). 2 expressions in all; Workers Paid allows 250 Cron Triggers per account (CF docs, verified
      // 2026-09-30), while the Durable Objects alarms page speaks of up to three, so as built Phase 5 adds none (D-3).
      "crons": [
        // Phase 4 (P4-2). Mirror table feature_flags to KV FLAGS every minute; drift report at minute 0.
        // Phase 5 (as built, PLAN.md §5.5 DV5-2): the same tick evaluates the schedule table of
        // workers/ops/src/cron/schedule.ts (UTC, own matcher, day of week 0 = Sunday) and only opens runs, creates
        // Workflow instances and sends queue messages: reddit tier1 */15, tier2 */30, tier3 hourly; hn */30;
        // tenders 06:00; Xometry 0 6,8,10,12,14,16,18; content-daily 07:00; sitemap 09:00 (stage S4 only);
        // ops-digest Monday 06:30; marketing follow-ups :05 hourly and warm-up 00:05 (vars). Each job is gated by
        // its flag (or var) and runs once per slot, so switch-over and rollback are flag flips, and the matching
        // pg_cron job (or the GitHub Action schedule) is deactivated in the same step (P5-8).
        "* * * * *",
        // Phase 4. Dispatcher: Gmail reply poller for the 2 Workspace sender accounts (P4-8, live 2026-09-30),
        // inbound rows left received, portal orders without a post-order run, parked runs, old failure cards,
        // stuck CAD jobs.
        "*/10 * * * *"
      ]
    },

    // Phase 4 (P4-11). Remote MCP on a Custom Domain (Cloudflare creates the DNS record and certificate;
    // CF docs, verified 2026-09-27). Active in workers/ops/wrangler.jsonc since the Phase 4 build, so the first
    // deploy with it waits for the zone (OW-5) and the Worker "None" route for mcp.micronshub.eu/* described under
    // microns-site "routes". An Access "MCP server" application with Managed OAuth protects it (OW-15); no grant
    // store in the Worker.
    "routes": [
      { "pattern": "mcp.micronshub.eu", "custom_domain": true }
    ]
  },

  // ===================================================================================================
  // microns-mail: Email Worker for rfq.micronshub.eu
  // ===================================================================================================
  "workers/mail/wrangler.jsonc": {
    "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
    "name": "microns-mail",
    // Exports email() only. Email Routing on the subdomain rfq.micronshub.eu sends rfq@ and replies@ here
    // (P4-4). Raw MIME goes to R2, one inbound_emails row is written, then the mail is handed to microns-ops
    // through OPS (rfq@: startIntake; replies@: ingestReply). Steps M0-M7: workers/mail/README.md.
    // The routing rules are set in the dashboard, so there are no routes. Apex MX stays untouched.
    "main": "src/index.ts",
    "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
    // As built the Worker parses headers only (no MIME library) and hashes the Message-ID with Web Crypto.
    "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
    // No HTTP surface.
    "workers_dev": false,
    "preview_urls": false,
    "observability": {
      "enabled": true,
      "head_sampling_rate": 1
    },

    "vars": {
      // Recipients accepted; anything else is refused with setReject(). Catch-all rules exist only on the
      // apex (CF docs, verified 2026-09-27), so both are explicit Email Routing addresses.
      "ALLOWED_RCPT": "rfq@rfq.micronshub.eu,replies@rfq.micronshub.eu",
      // Needed to write the inbound_emails row (ARCHITECTURE.md §7.3).
      "SUPABASE_URL": "https://cfjrtmtaitwzggzpkhxi.supabase.co",
      // Phase 4. Tenant of the inbound_emails rows (default tenant).
      "AGENT_TENANT_ID": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"
    },

    "r2_buckets": [
      // Phase 4. email/<message_id_sha256>/raw.eml and email/<message_id_sha256>/att/<n>-<name>. Same
      // jurisdiction as every other binding of the bucket.
      { "binding": "PRIVATE_FILES", "bucket_name": "microns-private", "jurisdiction": "eu" }
    ],

    "services": [
      // Phase 4. Named entrypoint MailIngest (RPC startIntake, ingestReply, ids only): the mail Worker never uses
      // OpsApi, which carries the /api calls of the site (DC-2). microns-ops is deployed first.
      { "binding": "OPS", "service": "microns-ops", "entrypoint": "MailIngest" }
    ],

    "secrets": {
      "required": [
        // Phase 4. Writes the inbound_emails row. MAIL_COPY_TO and MAIL_FALLBACK_TO are optional and checked per mail.
        "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"
      ]
    }
  }
}
